IPPON SHEET GLASS CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASANO OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INOUE HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASANO, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A glass panel comprising a pair of sheets (1A, 1B) of flat glass provided with their sheet surfaces opposite to each other, a clearance (V) formed between the sheets, and low-melting point glass (3) which bonds the peripheral edges of the sheets together to seal the clearance, wherein a roughened surface (8) extending along the almost entire peripheral edges is formed on the surfaces (5), to be bonded by the low-melting point glass, of the sheets.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce panneau vitré comprend une paire de feuilles (1A, 1B) de verre plat, dont les surfaces de feuille sont opposées l'une à l'autre, un espace intermédiaire (V) formé entre les feuilles, un verre (3) à bas point de fusion, lequel fixe ensemble les bords périphériques des feuilles afin de sceller l'espace intermédiaire, et il est caractérisé en ce qu'une surface rugueuse s'étendant le long de pratiquement tous ses bords périphériques est formée sur les surfaces (5) des feuilles, de manière que ces surfaces soient fixées par le verre à bas point de fusion.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicab